  "schema": "trueopen-dispatch-compensation-v1",
  "notes": [
    "Consumer state-transition acceptance cases; wire owns their public shapes and normative identities, not Keeper business logic.",
    "Claim primary is (session_id, order_sequence); ticket lookup is derived. A dismissed replacement removes old ticket/prune indexes atomically.",
    "Amounts are atomic units. PAID consumes the unique sequence allowance even when actual payment is zero; DISMISSED does not.",
    "Session lifecycle reads its fixed Task parameter version. All arithmetic is checked and cleanup is bounded by visited items.",
    "Each claim_cases row overrides claim_defaults; existing status and exact replay always refer to an existing claim row."
